    "statement": "Patchboard manages reversible overlays on object attributes.\n\nThere are `N` objects and `K` permanently existing attribute cells. A cell stores either an integer (`I x`) or an object reference (`O x`).\n\nA path consists of a root object and `L >= 1` attribute numbers. Starting at the root, read and follow the object reference in every attribute except the last; the last attribute identifies the target cell. Paths are resolved when used, against the current state.\n\nEach activation now contains an ordered transaction of `M >= 1` replacements. On `START`, process its replacements from first to last. For each replacement, resolve its path after all preceding replacements in that same activation have been applied, remember the identified cell and its current value, then write the replacement value. After all replacements, append the activation ID to the global activation order. The ID is guaranteed inactive before `START`, but may be reused after stopping.\n\n`STOP id` does nothing if `id` is inactive. Otherwise, restore that activation's remembered writes in reverse replacement order, then remove it from the global activation order. Each restoration writes the remembered value even if ano",
